DOCSTRINGS INSTRUCT FUNCTION -- they do not keep a record. Cody, 2026-08-15:
"docstrings don't keep truth, they instruct function." The test is not "is
this accurate" but "does this make the CALLER do the right thing". Imperative
register, not descriptive. So they are exempt from historical precedent:
replace an out-of-date docstring outright, in ANY code, without asking, and
never append "formerly X" / "renamed on DATE" -- a changelog does not
instruct. KEEP a warning when it steers the caller; a warning IS an
instruction. In this repo's terms: a docstring is a DATUM (definitional,
self-contained, no last-time); a wiki page is a BEARING (relational, holds
the record, retractions load-bearing).

